#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""hack-box overlay: the attendee-facing face of the session engine.

Runs as the attendee inside the Cinnamon session (autostarted from the
skeleton, relaunched by hackbox-guard if killed). It is only a display: it
reads the state that root writes to /run/hackbox and asks systemd (through
the polkit rule) to start the session timer or the reset. Killing it changes
nothing about the clock.

Faces, by /run/hackbox/state (SPEC 3.2 and 3.6):
  idle       full-screen welcome, rules, one Start button per agent
             (with a hub: the attendee's name first)
  active     small always-on-top countdown pill with "End now"
             (with a hub: "More time", which asks the staff)
  ending     full-screen "Time is up" with the archive code
             (with a hub: QR code and link to download, and Done)
  resetting  full-screen "Resetting"

Python 3 and GTK 3 through gi only (both ship with Mint Cinnamon). No GL.
"""

